# App rules — <app> (TEMPLATE)

Copy this file to `rules/<app>.md` (gitignored, like your `configs/<app>.json`)
and replace the examples below with your app's real rules. Point your config's
`target.rulesFile` (and optionally `platforms.<p>.rulesFile`) at it.

App-wide operational knowledge injected into EVERY spoke for this app. This is
the spoke's ONLY knowledge of these quirks, so each rule must be true and
self-contained. Device-input rules (e.g. how a focused field is SUBMITTED) live
on the DeviceProfile, NOT here.

## Auth

Where your test credentials live and how to sign in. Example:

> The test credentials are in the file at the PI env path `envTest`. Call the
> `read_creds` tool to read them when you need to sign in — never guess or invent
> credentials. Use the `app` verb's `cold-reset` for a true signed-out first run
> before testing the sign-in flow.

## Quirk: <one-line title>

Describe an app behavior the spoke cannot derive just by observing, written as a
procedure it can follow. Example:

> Focusing any text field spawns a NEW field docked above the on-screen keyboard,
> so the `@ref` from your previous `observe` is STALE. After you focus a field,
> re-run `observe`, find the newly-docked field, and `type` into THAT ref — never
> into the original one (typing there silently does nothing the guards can catch).
